TabPad Privacy Policy

Effective date: 19 October 2026

TabPad is a text editor for iPhone and iPad, developed by Darren Wilson ("I", "me"). This policy explains what happens to your information when you use TabPad.

The short version: TabPad doesn't collect, store, or share any of your personal information. Your documents stay on your device, or wherever you choose to put them. I can't see them, and neither can anyone else.

What TabPad does not do

	•	❌ No accounts or sign-up
	•	❌ No analytics or usage tracking
	•	❌ No advertising
	•	❌ No selling or sharing of data with anyone
	•	❌ No servers. TabPad doesn't send your documents or personal information to me or to any third party.

Your documents

	•	New documents are saved on your device, in TabPad's own folder (visible in the Files app under On My iPhone/iPad › TabPad).
	•	If you use Move to… to put a document in iCloud Drive, Dropbox, or another location, it's stored by that service under its privacy policy and terms. TabPad only reads and writes the file where you put it.
	•	Files you open from other apps are accessed only with your permission, and only for editing.

Settings

Your preferences, such as tabs or sidebar and your default file format, plus the list of files you had open, are stored on your device only so TabPad can restore your workspace next time.

Reminders

TabPad can remind you about a file at a date and time, or when you arrive at or leave a place.

	•	Notifications: reminders are local notifications, scheduled and delivered by iOS on your device. Nothing is sent to me or to a server.
	•	Location: TabPad asks for location access only if you choose to create a location-based reminder. Your location is monitored by iOS on your device to trigger the reminder. TabPad does not record, store, or send your location anywhere.
	•	Place search: when you search for a place while setting up a location reminder, the search is handled by Apple Maps (MapKit). Those searches are covered by Apple's privacy policy.

You can turn off notifications or location access at any time in the iOS Settings app. TabPad keeps working, just without those reminders.

Children

TabPad doesn't collect personal information from anyone, including children under 13.

Changes to this policy
If this policy changes, the updated version will be posted on this page with a new effective date.

